---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import BrandMark from '../components/BrandMark.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/brand';

const updated = new Date('2026-08-26T00:00:00Z');
const updatedLabel = new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-GB', {
  day: 'numeric',
  month: 'short',
  year: 'numeric',
  timeZone: 'UTC',
}).format(updated);
---

<Base
  title="Terms & Privacy"
  description={`Terms of use and privacy policy for ${site.name}, operated by ${site.legalName} (ABN ${site.abn}).`}
  canonical="/terms"
>
  <main id="content" class="article-page">
    <BrandMark class="panel-mark" />
    <header class="article-header">
      <time datetime={updated.toISOString()}>Updated {updatedLabel}</time>
      <h1>Terms &amp; Privacy</h1>
      <p>
        Two short documents for this website: how you may use it, and what we do if you write to
        us.
      </p>
      <nav class="legal-toc" aria-label="On this page">
        <a href="#terms-of-use">Terms of use</a>
        <a href="#privacy-policy">Privacy policy</a>
      </nav>
    </header>
    <article class="article-body prose">
      <p>
        This page applies to the public website at <a href={site.url}>{site.url.replace('https://', '')}</a>
        {' '}(the <strong>site</strong>), including the project catalogue and the notes. It is issued by{' '}
        {site.legalName} (ABN {site.abn}) (<strong>we</strong>, <strong>us</strong>, <strong>our</strong>),
        an Australian sole trader business, trading as {site.name}.
      </p>

      <h2 id="terms-of-use">Terms of use</h2>

      <h3>What this site is</h3>
      <p>
        {site.name} publishes open source software. This site is a brand landing, a live catalogue
        of public repositories under the{' '}
        <a href={site.githubUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">MajestaNet GitHub organisation</a>,
        and a notebook of notes. It is not a hosted software service, a marketplace, or a place where
        we sell goods.
      </p>
      <p>
        Reading the site is free. There are no accounts, subscriptions, or support contracts offered
        through these pages. Using the site does not create a professional-services or support
        relationship with us.
      </p>

      <h3>This website is not the software</h3>
      <p>
        This website — including its source, notes, article media, and brand artwork — is proprietary.
        Viewing the published site or the public GitHub tree does not grant you a licence to copy,
        modify, or reuse that material, except as copyright law already allows. See the website
        repository{' '}
        <a href={`${site.githubWebsiteUrl}/blob/main/LICENSE`}>LICENSE</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Open source projects listed on the site are published in separate repositories. Each
        project’s licence, contribution terms, and disclaimers are in that repository. Those licence
        terms govern that software. If these terms of use and a project’s licence conflict, the
        project’s licence prevails for that software.
      </p>

      <h3>Notes</h3>
      <p>
        Notes are general information and opinion. They are not legal, financial, security, or other
        professional advice. They may be incomplete or become out of date. Do not rely on them as
        the basis for a decision. Links to other sites are for convenience; we do not control those
        sites and we are not responsible for them.
      </p>

      <h3>Open source projects</h3>
      <p>
        Software in MajestaNet repositories is offered under the licence stated in the relevant
        repository, usually on an “as is” basis and without warranty, to the extent the law allows.
        You decide whether to use it, and you must comply with its licence. We are not obliged to
        maintain, patch, host, or support any project unless we agree with you in writing.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you contribute to a project, you do that on GitHub, under that repository’s licence and
        GitHub’s terms — not through this site.
      </p>

      <h3>Our name and artwork</h3>
      <p>
        The {site.name} name, wordmarks, globe symbol, and other brand artwork are our trade marks.
        You may not use them except with our written permission, or as the law already permits (for
        example, a fair reference to the software or to this site).
      </p>

      <h3>Acceptable use</h3>
      <p>
        Use the site only for ordinary browsing and reading. Do not attempt to disrupt it, overload
        it, or use it for anything unlawful. If you find a security issue, email{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> as described in our{' '}
        <a href={`${site.githubWebsiteUrl}/blob/main/SECURITY.md`}>security policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h3>Hosting and GitHub</h3>
      <p>
        The site is hosted by Netlify. The home page asks GitHub’s public API from your browser for
        the organisation’s public repositories. Netlify and GitHub have their own terms. We are not
        responsible for their services, availability, or policies.
      </p>

      <h3>Liability</h3>
      <p>
        Nothing in these terms excludes, restricts, or modifies any consumer guarantee, right, or
        remedy conferred by the Australian Consumer Law or any other law that cannot lawfully be
        excluded.
      </p>
      <p>To the maximum extent permitted by law:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          the site, the notes, and any software are provided as is, without warranties of any kind,
          including fitness for a particular purpose and non-infringement;
        </li>
        <li>
          we are not liable for any loss or damage arising from your use of, or inability to use,
          the site, the notes, or any project, including indirect or consequential loss, loss of
          data, or loss of profit; and
        </li>
        <li>
          if we are liable to you and that liability cannot be excluded, our liability is limited to,
          at our option, re-supplying the relevant services or paying the cost of having them
          supplied again.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Changes</h3>
      <p>
        We may change the site and these terms. The current version is the one on this page.
        If you keep using the site after a change, you accept the updated terms.
      </p>

      <h3>Law</h3>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of Victoria, Australia. That choice of law does not
        take away any right you cannot contract out of where you live. If a dispute is heard in
        court, the courts of Victoria may hear it.
      </p>

      <h3>Contact</h3>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="privacy-policy">Privacy policy</h2>

      <h3>Who we are</h3>
      <p>
        {site.legalName} (ABN {site.abn}) operates this site. For privacy questions, email{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h3>What we collect — and what we do not</h3>
      <p>
        We may only collect and retain your email address if you enquire directly via this site and
        its listed contact details. Today that means writing to{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. If you send a message, we will also have
        whatever you choose to put in it (for example your name, or a GitHub handle).
      </p>
      <p>
        There are no accounts, newsletters, contact forms, advertising pixels, or analytics scripts
        on these pages. We do not set first-party cookies. Ordinary browsing does not give us your
        email address.
      </p>
      <p>
        Your browser may keep a short-lived copy of the public GitHub repository list in session
        storage so the project catalogue need not ask GitHub on every visit. That copy stays on your
        device. We do not receive it.
      </p>

      <h3>How we use an enquiry</h3>
      <p>
        If you email us, we use that correspondence only to read and respond to your enquiry, and to
        keep an ordinary business record of it. We do not use your email for marketing. We do not
        sell it. We do not add you to a list.
      </p>
      <p>
        We keep it only for as long as we reasonably need it for that enquiry and those records,
        then we delete it from our records. If you ask us to delete it sooner, we will, unless we
        are required by law to keep a copy.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you contact the MajestaNet organisation on GitHub instead, GitHub handles that under its
        own terms and privacy statement. That is not a collection by this site.
      </p>

      <h3>Hosting, GitHub, and email</h3>
      <p>
        Netlify hosts the site. Their infrastructure may process technical request data (such as IP
        address, browser type, and timestamps) in order to serve the pages and keep them secure. See{' '}
        <a href="https://www.netlify.com/privacy/">Netlify’s privacy policy</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        The home page requests GitHub’s public API from your browser. That request is made by your
        browser to GitHub, not through our servers, and is subject to{' '}
        <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub’s privacy statement</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Those providers may store or process information outside Australia, including in the United
        States. If you email us, your message also passes through our email provider, which may be
        outside Australia. We do not control those systems.
      </p>

      <h3>Who we disclose to</h3>
      <p>We do not disclose your email address except:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>to our email and hosting providers, as needed to operate the site and receive mail;</li>
        <li>if the law requires us to; or</li>
        <li>if you ask us to.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Changes</h3>
      <p>
        We may update this policy. The current version is the one on this page. If we start
        collecting more than enquiry email, we will say so here before we do.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
